<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lü Jia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 111 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lü Jia was chancellor of the kingdom of Nanyue in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, serving several of its kings over decades. In 112 BCE, opposing the plan of the queen dowager and the young king Zhao Xing to submit to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, he killed them and the Han envoys and enthroned Zhao Jiande. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu of Han</a> responded by invading, and in 111 BCE Han forces took the capital Panyu and captured Lü Jia, ending Nanyue's independence.</p></div>
